rem An error inside a half-typed block must abandon THAT block and nothing else:
rem the session keeps its variables and functions, and the next line runs. The
rem error text goes to stderr and is not part of this transcript -- what stdout
rem proves is the recovery, which is the part a person depends on.
kept = 5
function twice(n)
return n * 2
endfunction
for i% = 1 to 2
println @@@
next
println "the variable survived: " + str$(kept)
println "and so did the function: " + str$(twice(21))
for j% = 1 to 2
println "and a good block still works: " + str$(j%)
next
